  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$\n\nThe only number that satisfies this definition is $7.$ It has only two factors: $1$ and $7.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =1\\times 7 \\\\  & =7\\times 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll the other given numbers have at least one factor distinct from itself, and $1:$\n\n- $21$ has $3$ and $7$ as factors:\n\n$$\n21=3\\times 7\n$$\n\n- $9$ has $3$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n9=3\\times 3\n$$\n\n- $24$ has $3$ and $8$ as factors:\n\n$$\n24=3\\times 8\n$$\n\n- $15$ has $3$ and $5$ as factors:\n\n$$\n15=3\\times 5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $7.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
